# a-wave-screened-by-four — plan 23 K3, the TWIN.
#
# The same twelve robots into the same sealed band, with four of them
# swapped for the weakest class in the game — and the wall does not
# open at all.
#
# ── Read it beside its twin ─────────────────────────────────────
#
# `a-wave-of-twelve-miners.keys` is this file with
#
#     compose 0 4 scout 8 miner      ->      compose 0 12 miner
#
# and nothing else.  That file's base is gone in **94 ticks**.  This
# one still has 100 HP on every hex the siege can reach after fifty,
# and `23_k3` measures it standing at 321 — the longest base anybody
# can play (`@M005`).
#
# ⚠⚠ **Two thirds of this wave is miners**, at 3.0 HP/s each, the
# hardest-biting class in the game.  Not one of them lays a finger on
# the wall.
#
# ── Why: three shipped rules, and none of them is wrong ─────────
#
#   1. **The siege front is the approach FAN's width, not the wall's**
#      (plan 12 B3).  Exactly three hexes of this five-row wall are
#      ever attacked — (6,-2), (6, 0) and (6, 1) — and a seven-row
#      wall does not add a fourth.
#   2. **An enemy blocked by a COMPANION attacks nothing** (plan 11
#      F7b).  It steps beside if it can and stands if it cannot; what
#      it never does is chew over its neighbour's shoulder.
#   3. **Speed decides who gets there first** (plan 23 K2b).  A scout
#      walks 2.5 hex/s against a miner's 1.0, so the scouts arrive
#      first whatever order the roster put them in.
#
# So the four fastest robots in the wave fill all three attack hexes,
# and the eight behind them stand in a field for the rest of the run.
#
# ⚠ **The missing rule is already named** — the equal-distance
# sidestep that would let a besieger spread ALONG a wall face instead
# of queueing behind the hex its route landed on.  `ENEMY_MOVEMENT.md`
# and `CLAUDE.md` have both carried it as latent since plan 11 F7.
# This pair is what it costs.
#
# ── The world (identical to its twin) ───────────────────────────
#
#   five rows of grass, twenty-four columns:  (-3, -2) .. (20, 2)
#   sealed at q = 6 with a wall across all five rows
#   core at (0, 0), spawn at (14, 0) facing west

echo four scouts in front: the miners never reach the wall

do toggle_mode

# The core is where the target is.
do cycle_kind
click 0 0
marker 0 0 target

# The spawn, fourteen hexes east — clear of close_spawn_disable_radius
# (10) and well inside the scrambler bubble (25).
# ⚠ TWICE more: the place-kind cycle is spawn -> target -> tower ->
# spawn since plan 12 B5a gave towers a marker kind of their own.
do cycle_kind
do cycle_kind
do rotate
do rotate
do rotate
click 14 0
marker 14 0 spawn 3

count markers 2 2
do toggle_mode

palette 5
drag -3 -2 20 -2
drag -3 -1 20 -1
drag -3 0 20 0
drag -3 1 20 1
drag -3 2 20 2
count painted 120 120

palette 9
click 6 -2
click 6 -1
click 6 0
click 6 1
click 6 2
kind 6 0 wall
count painted 120 120

# ── The wave, composed — and this is the only line that differs ──
#
# ⚠ The order written is the order spawned (plan 23 K1), so the four
# scouts leave first here.  It makes no difference: § The roster order
# is worth nothing in `23_k3` measures the same twelve with the scouts
# LAST and with them alternated through the miners, and all three land
# on the same tick.  Speed is the order now.
schedule 12
compose 0 4 scout 8 miner
pending 0 0.0 15.0 on
waves 0 0
count alive 0 0

tick 1
waves 1 1
count alive 12 12
enemy 0 14 0

# ── Nine ticks: standing, and the wall is untouched ─────────────
tick 9
hp 6 0 100.0 100.0
hp 6 -2 30.0 30.0
count targets 0 0

# ── Thirty ticks: its twin's wall is two thirds gone ────────────
#
# At this exact tick `a-wave-of-twelve-miners.keys` reads 10 HP on
# (6,-2) and 78 on (6, 0).  Here the end has lost **one point** and the
# middle has lost one — because the three robots on the face are
# scouts, at 0.1 HP/s against a miner's 3.0.
tick 20
count targets 3 3
hp 6 -2 28.5 29.5
hp 6 0 98.5 99.5
hp 6 -1 100.0 100.0

# ── Forty ticks: the formation, and it never changes again ──────
#
# ⚠ **The whole finding is these six lines.**  The four scouts hold
# (7,-2), (7, 0), (7, 2) and (7,-1) — every hex from which the wall can
# be reached — and the miners are stacked behind them at q = 8 and
# q = 9 with nothing to attack.  Enemies 0-3 are the scouts, 4-11 the
# miners, in the order `compose` wrote them.
tick 10
enemy 0 7 -2
enemy 1 7 0
enemy 2 7 2
enemy 3 7 -1
enemy 5 8 0
enemy 11 9 -2
count targets 3 3

snap k3-four-scouts-screen-eight-miners

# ── Fifty ticks, and nothing has moved ──────────────────────────
#
# ⚠ The wall is still a wall, the roster is still twelve, and the
# wallet is still full — its twin's base fell forty-four ticks ago.
# The siege is not slow here, it is HAPPENING: three hexes are under
# attack every tick.  They are just under attack by scouts.
tick 10
kind 6 -2 wall
kind 6 0 wall
count alive 12 12
count targets 3 3
enemy 0 7 -2
enemy 5 8 0
wallet 200.0 200.0
